{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_14hY6Ly5hdllWRZJDc64jafV","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# human-as-mcp Specification\n     2→\n     3→## Purpose\n     4→Define the Human-as-MCP interface for obtaining human input on-demand. This spec governs sync and async human call modes, call persistence, non-blocking execution, and the first-time bootstrap flow where project intent is captured directly from human input without pre-written requirement files.\n     5→## Requirements\n     6→### Requirement: Human Call Interface\n     7→The system SHALL define a standard human call interface supporting sync and async modes.\n     8→\n     9→**Sync mode** (human present):\n    10→- Ask directly via Claude Code conversation (AskUserQuestion)\n    11→- Use for: immediate decisions, requirement clarification, project direction\n    12→\n    13→**Async mode** (human unavailable):\n    14→- Write request file to `human-calls/`\n    15→- Use for: offline operations, cross-session pending requests\n    16→\n    17→**First-time bootstrap**: When entering an empty project, the agent SHALL ask the human \"What should this project do?\" via sync human call, then create an openspec change directly from the response. The change proposal captures the human's intent; specs formalize it. No intermediate demands file.\n    18→\n    19→#### Scenario: Sync call — first-time project intent\n    20→- **WHEN** agent enters an empty project\n    21→- **THEN** agent asks the human via sync call, creates an openspec change proposal from the response\n    22→\n    23→#### Scenario: Sync call — immediate decision\n    24→- **WHEN** agent needs a human decision and the human is present\n    25→- **THEN** agent asks directly via conversation\n    26→\n    27→#### Scenario: Async call — offline operation\n    28→- **WHEN** agent needs the human to perform an operation that requires offline time\n    29→- **THEN** agent writes a request to human-calls/, marks dependent tasks as waiting-human\n    30→\n    31→#### Scenario: Human responds to async call\n    32→- **WHEN** a human fills in the Response section of a pending request\n    33→- **THEN** next session processes the response and unblocks dependent work\n    34→\n    35→### Requirement: Non-Blocking Execution\n    36→Human calls MUST NOT block unrelated tasks.\n    37→\n    38→#### Scenario: Continue after issuing call\n    39→- **WHEN** agent issues a human call and other independent tasks exist\n    40→- **THEN** agent marks dependent tasks as waiting-human and continues other work\n    41→\n    42→### Requirement: Human Call Persistence\n    43→Async human call requests SHALL be persisted to the file system.\n    44→\n    45→Files stored in `human-calls/` with filename format `{YYYYMMDD}-{HHmmss}-{short-description}.md`.\n    46→\n    47→#### Scenario: Cross-session persistence\n    48→- **WHEN** session A's human call is unanswered at session end\n    49→- **THEN** the file persists and session B checks for responses on startup\n    50→\n    51→### Requirement: Human Call Types\n    52→The system SHALL support three types: decision, action, information.\n    53→\n    54→#### Scenario: Decision call\n    55→- **WHEN** agent needs the human to choose between options\n    56→- **THEN** the call lists all options with trade-off analysis\n    57→\n    58→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fda141f5-a3a9-4f60-9302-36b25383cb2b","uuid":"3ab0d648-bb6d-4119-a018-376d5e3ea6d0","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/data/cre/workspace/se3.0/.worktrees/human-input-methods/openspec/specs/human-as-mcp/spec.md","content":"# human-as-mcp Specification\n\n## Purpose\nDefine the Human-as-MCP interface for obtaining human input on-demand. This spec governs sync and async human call modes, call persistence, non-blocking execution, and the first-time bootstrap flow where project intent is captured directly from human input without pre-written requirement files.\n## Requirements\n### Requirement: Human Call Interface\nThe system SHALL define a standard human call interface supporting sync and async modes.\n\n**Sync mode** (human present):\n- Ask directly via Claude Code conversation (AskUserQuestion)\n- Use for: immediate decisions, requirement clarification, project direction\n\n**Async mode** (human unavailable):\n- Write request file to `human-calls/`\n- Use for: offline operations, cross-session pending requests\n\n**First-time bootstrap**: When entering an empty project, the agent SHALL ask the human \"What should this project do?\" via sync human call, then create an openspec change directly from the response. The change proposal captures the human's intent; specs formalize it. No intermediate demands file.\n\n#### Scenario: Sync call — first-time project intent\n- **WHEN** agent enters an empty project\n- **THEN** agent asks the human via sync call, creates an openspec change proposal from the response\n\n#### Scenario: Sync call — immediate decision\n- **WHEN** agent needs a human decision and the human is present\n- **THEN** agent asks directly via conversation\n\n#### Scenario: Async call — offline operation\n- **WHEN** agent needs the human to perform an operation that requires offline time\n- **THEN** agent writes a request to human-calls/, marks dependent tasks as waiting-human\n\n#### Scenario: Human responds to async call\n- **WHEN** a human fills in the Response section of a pending request\n- **THEN** next session processes the response and unblocks dependent work\n\n### Requirement: Non-Blocking Execution\nHuman calls MUST NOT block unrelated tasks.\n\n#### Scenario: Continue after issuing call\n- **WHEN** agent issues a human call and other independent tasks exist\n- **THEN** agent marks dependent tasks as waiting-human and continues other work\n\n### Requirement: Human Call Persistence\nAsync human call requests SHALL be persisted to the file system.\n\nFiles stored in `human-calls/` with filename format `{YYYYMMDD}-{HHmmss}-{short-description}.md`.\n\n#### Scenario: Cross-session persistence\n- **WHEN** session A's human call is unanswered at session end\n- **THEN** the file persists and session B checks for responses on startup\n\n### Requirement: Human Call Types\nThe system SHALL support three types: decision, action, information.\n\n#### Scenario: Decision call\n- **WHEN** agent needs the human to choose between options\n- **THEN** the call lists all options with trade-off analysis\n\n","numLines":58,"startLine":1,"totalLines":58}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_z9jtQzssInS9k2HX79oHIERQ","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→\"\"\"Human calls detection and processing module for SE 3.0.\n     2→\n     3→Provides optimized human call file handling with:\n     4→- Structured storage format with frontmatter\n     5→- Efficient change-based detection using file timestamps\n     6→- Response integrity validation\n     7→- Multi-language support\n     8→\"\"\"\n     9→\n    10→import re\n    11→import os\n    12→import json\n    13→from dataclasses import dataclass, field, asdict\n    14→from datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\n    15→from enum import Enum\n    16→from pathlib import Path\n    17→from typing import Dict, List, Optional, Any, Callable, Set, Tuple\n    18→import hashlib\n    19→\n    20→\n    21→class CallStatus(Enum):\n    22→    \"\"\"Human call status states.\"\"\"\n    23→    PENDING = \"pending\"\n    24→    RESPONDED = \"responded\"\n    25→    PROCESSING = \"processing\"\n    26→    COMPLETED = \"completed\"\n    27→    EXPIRED = \"expired\"\n    28→\n    29→\n    30→class CallType(Enum):\n    31→    \"\"\"Human call types.\"\"\"\n    32→    DECISION = \"decision\"\n    33→    ACTION = \"action\"\n    34→    INFORMATION = \"information\"\n    35→    ESCALATION = \"escalation\"\n    36→\n    37→\n    38→class CallPriority(Enum):\n    39→    \"\"\"Human call priority levels.\"\"\"\n    40→    LOW = \"low\"\n    41→    MEDIUM = \"medium\"\n    42→    HIGH = \"high\"\n    43→    CRITICAL = \"critical\"\n    44→\n    45→\n    46→@dataclass\n    47→class HumanCall:\n    48→    \"\"\"Represents a human call with metadata and content.\n    49→\n    50→    Attributes:\n    51→        id: Unique identifier for the call\n    52→        file_path: Path to the call file\n    53→        call_type: Type of call (decision, action, information, escalation)\n    54→        priority: Priority level\n    55→        status: Current status\n    56→        created: Creation timestamp\n    57→        source: Source component (e.g., collab-orchestrator, worker)\n    58→        title: Call title/subject\n    59→        context: Call context/description\n    60→        response: Human response content\n    61→        response_timestamp: When response was received\n    62→        metadata: Additional metadata\n    63→    \"\"\"\n    64→    id: str\n    65→    file_path: Path\n    66→    call_type: CallType = CallType.ACTION\n    67→    priority: CallPriority = CallPriority.MEDIUM\n    68→    status: CallStatus = CallStatus.PENDING\n    69→    created: datetime = field(default_factory=datetime.now)\n    70→    source: str = \"unknown\"\n    71→    title: str = \"\"\n    72→    context: str = \"\"\n    73→    response: str = \"\"\n    74→    response_timestamp: Optional[datetime] = None\n    75→    metadata: Dict[str, Any] = field(default_factory=dict)\n    76→\n    77→    def to_dict(self) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    78→        \"\"\"Convert to dictionary for serialization.\"\"\"\n    79→        return {\n    80→            \"id\": self.id,\n    81→            \"file_path\": str(self.file_path),\n    82→            \"type\": self.call_type.value,\n    83→            \"priority\": self.priority.value,\n    84→            \"status\": self.status.value,\n    85→            \"created\": self.created.isoformat(),\n    86→            \"source\": self.source,\n    87→            \"title\": self.title,\n    88→            \"context\": self.context,\n    89→            \"response\": self.response,\n    90→            \"response_timestamp\": self.response_timestamp.isoformat() if self.response_timestamp else None,\n    91→            \"metadata\": self.metadata,\n    92→        }\n    93→\n    94→    @classmethod\n    95→    def from_dict(cls, data: Dict[str, Any]) -> \"HumanCall\":\n    96→        \"\"\"Create from dictionary.\"\"\"\n    97→        return cls(\n    98→            id=data[\"id\"],\n    99→            file_path=Path(data[\"file_path\"]),\n   100→            call_type=CallType(data.get(\"type\", \"action\")),\n   101→            priority=CallPriority(data.get(\"priority\", \"medium\")),\n   102→            status=CallStatus(data.get(\"status\", \"pending\")),\n   103→            created=datetime.fromisoformat(data[\"created\"]) if \"created\" in data else datetime.now(),\n   104→            source=data.get(\"source\", \"unknown\"),\n   105→            title=data.get(\"title\", \"\"),\n   106→            context=data.get(\"context\", \"\"),\n   107→            response=data.get(\"response\", \"\"),\n   108→            response_timestamp=datetime.fromisoformat(data[\"response_timestamp\"]) if data.get(\"response_timestamp\") else None,\n   109→            metadata=data.get(\"metadata\", {}),\n   110→        )\n   111→\n   112→\n   113→class HumanCallStore:\n   114→    \"\"\"Manages human call files with optimized detection.\n   115→\n   116→    Features:\n   117→    - Efficient change detection using file system events and caching\n   118→    - Structured frontmatter format\n   119→    - Comprehensive response integrity validation\n   120→    - Multi-language support\n   121→    - Batch processing capabilities\n   122→    \"\"\"\n   123→\n   124→    # File patterns\n   125→    CALL_FILE_PATTERN = \"*.md\"\n   126→    RESPONDED_SUFFIX = \".responded\"\n   127→    PROCESSING_SUFFIX = \".processing\"\n   128→    COMPLETED_SUFFIX = \".completed\"\n   129→\n   130→    # Response section headers (multi-language)\n   131→    RESPONSE_HEADERS = [\"### Response\", \"### 回复\", \"### Réponse\"]\n   132→    CONTEXT_HEADERS = [\"### Context\", \"### 上下文\", \"### Contexte\"]\n   133→\n   134→    # Default prompt markers that indicate no response yet\n   135→    DEFAULT_PROMPT_MARKERS = [\n   136→        \"<!-- Human: write your response below -->\",\n   137→        \"<!-- 人类：请在下方输入您的回复 -->\",\n   138→        \"<!-- Humain: écrivez votre réponse ci-dessous -->\",\n   139→    ]\n   140→\n   141→    # Minimum response requirements\n   142→    MIN_RESPONSE_LENGTH = 10\n   143→    MIN_MEANINGFUL_CHARS = 5\n   144→    MAX_RESPONSE_LENGTH = 10000\n   145→\n   146→    def __init__(self, calls_dir: Path):\n   147→        \"\"\"Initialize the store.\n   148→\n   149→        Args:\n   150→            calls_dir: Directory containing human call files\n   151→        \"\"\"\n   152→        self.calls_dir = Path(calls_dir)\n   153→        self.calls_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n   154→\n   155→        # State tracking for efficient change detection\n   156→        self._last_scan_time: Optional[datetime] = None\n   157→        self._file_hashes: Dict[str, str] = {}\n   158→        self._file_mtimes: Dict[str, float] = {}\n   159→        self._call_cache: Dict[str, HumanCall] = {}\n   160→\n   161→        # Pre-scan to populate initial state\n   162→        self._initialize_cache()\n   163→\n   164→    def _initialize_cache(self):\n   165→        \"\"\"Initialize cache with existing call files.\"\"\"\n   166→        for filepath in self.calls_dir.glob(self.CALL_FILE_PATTERN):\n   167→            if filepath.is_file():\n   168→                path_str = str(filepath)\n   169→                self._file_mtimes[path_str] = filepath.stat().st_mtime\n   170→                self._file_hashes[path_str] = self._compute_file_hash(filepath)\n   171→                call = self.parse_call_file(filepath)\n   172→                if call:\n   173→                    self._call_cache[path_str] = call\n   174→        self._last_scan_time = datetime.now()\n   175→\n   176→    def _compute_file_hash(self, filepath: Path) -> str:\n   177→        \"\"\"Compute hash of file content for change detection.\n   178→\n   179→        Optimized to read only first 1KB for faster hash computation\n   180→        \"\"\"\n   181→        with open(filepath, 'rb') as f:\n   182→            content = f.read(1024)  # Read first 1KB for faster hashing\n   183→            return hashlib.sha256(content).hexdigest()[:16]\n   184→\n   185→    def _parse_frontmatter(self, content: str) -> Tuple[Dict[str, Any], str]:\n   186→        \"\"\"Parse YAML-like frontmatter from markdown content.\n   187→\n   188→        Returns:\n   189→            Tuple of (frontmatter dict, body content)\n   190→        \"\"\"\n   191→        frontmatter = {}\n   192→        body = content\n   193→\n   194→        # Match frontmatter between --- markers\n   195→        match = re.match(r'^---\\s*\\n(.*?)\\n---\\s*\\n(.*)', content, re.DOTALL)\n   196→        if match:\n   197→            fm_text = match.group(1)\n   198→            body = match.group(2)\n   199→\n   200→            # Parse key: value pairs\n   201→            for line in fm_text.strip().split('\\n'):\n   202→                if ':' in line:\n   203→                    key, value = line.split(':', 1)\n   204→                    frontmatter[key.strip()] = value.strip()\n   205→\n   206→        return frontmatter, body\n   207→\n   208→    def _extract_section(self, content: str, headers: List[str]) -> str:\n   209→        \"\"\"Extract content under a section header.\n   210→\n   211→        Args:\n   212→            content: Full markdown content\n   213→            headers: List of possible section headers to match\n   214→\n   215→        Returns:\n   216→            Section content or empty string if not found\n   217→        \"\"\"\n   218→        lines = content.split('\\n')\n   219→        in_section = False\n   220→        section_lines = []\n   221→\n   222→        for line in lines:\n   223→            # Check if this is the target section header\n   224→            if any(line.strip().startswith(header) for header in headers):\n   225→                in_section = True\n   226→                continue\n   227→\n   228→            # Check if we've reached the next section\n   229→            if in_section and line.strip().startswith('### '):\n   230→                break\n   231→\n   232→            if in_section:\n   233→                section_lines.append(line)\n   234→\n   235→        return '\\n'.join(section_lines).strip()\n   236→\n   237→    def _has_meaningful_response(self, content: str) -> bool:\n   238→        \"\"\"Check if content contains a meaningful human response.\n   239→\n   240→        Args:\n   241→            content: Response section content\n   242→\n   243→        Returns:\n   244→            True if response appears meaningful, False otherwise\n   245→        \"\"\"\n   246→        if not content:\n   247→            return False\n   248→\n   249→        # Check for default prompt markers (indicates no real response)\n   250→        for marker in self.DEFAULT_PROMPT_MARKERS:\n   251→            if marker in content:\n   252→                return False\n   253→\n   254→        # Check for HTML comments only (empty response)\n   255→        cleaned = re.sub(r'<!--.*?-->', '', content, flags=re.DOTALL).strip()\n   256→        if not cleaned:\n   257→            return False\n   258→\n   259→        # Check minimum meaningful content length (at least 10 chars)\n   260→        if len(cleaned) < 10:\n   261→            return False\n   262→\n   263→        return True\n   264→\n   265→    def _generate_call_id(self, title: str, timestamp: Optional[datetime] = None) -> str:\n   266→        \"\"\"Generate a unique call ID.\n   267→\n   268→        Format: {YYYYMMDD}-{HHmmss}-{short-description}\n   269→        \"\"\"\n   270→        ts = timestamp or datetime.now()\n   271→        # Clean title for filename\n   272→        clean_title = re.sub(r'[^\\w\\s-]', '', title.lower())\n   273→        clean_title = re.sub(r'[-\\s]+', '-', clean_title).strip('-')[:30]\n   274→        return f\"{ts.strftime('%Y%m%d-%H%M%S')}-{clean_title}\"\n   275→\n   276→    def create_call(\n   277→        self,\n   278→        title: str,\n   279→        context: str,\n   280→        call_type: CallType = CallType.ACTION,\n   281→        priority: CallPriority = CallPriority.MEDIUM,\n   282→        source: str = \"unknown\",\n   283→        language: str = \"en\",\n   284→        metadata: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None,\n   285→    ) -> HumanCall:\n   286→        \"\"\"Create a new human call file.\n   287→\n   288→        Args:\n   289→            title: Call title\n   290→            context: Call context/description\n   291→            call_type: Type of call\n   292→            priority: Priority level\n   293→            source: Source component\n   294→            language: Language code (en, zh, etc.)\n   295→            metadata: Additional metadata\n   296→\n   297→        Returns:\n   298→            Created HumanCall object\n   299→        \"\"\"\n   300→        call_id = self._generate_call_id(title)\n   301→        filepath = self.calls_dir / f\"{call_id}.md\"\n   302→\n   303→        # Load language labels from config module\n   304→        from .config import get_language_labels, is_chinese_language\n   305→        t = get_language_labels(language)\n   306→\n   307→        # Add language guidance for context content\n   308→        if is_chinese_language(language):\n   309→            language_note = \"\\n\\n**注意**：请用中文回复。\"\n   310→        else:\n   311→            language_note = \"\"\n   312→\n   313→        # Build frontmatter and content\n   314→        content = f\"\"\"---\n   315→id: {call_id}\n   316→type: {call_type.value}\n   317→priority: {priority.value}\n   318→status: pending\n   319→created: {datetime.now().isoformat()}\n   320→source: {source}\n   321→language: {language}\n   322→---\n   323→\n   324→## Request: {title}\n   325→\n   326→**{t['type']}**: {call_type.value}\n   327→**{t['urgency']}**: {priority.value}\n   328→**{t['source']}**: {source}\n   329→\n   330→### {t['context']}\n   331→{context}{language_note}\n   332→\n   333→### {t['response']}\n   334→{t['prompt']}\n   335→\"\"\"\n   336→\n   337→        filepath.write_text(content, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n   338→\n   339→        call = HumanCall(\n   340→            id=call_id,\n   341→            file_path=filepath,\n   342→            call_type=call_type,\n   343→            priority=priority,\n   344→            status=CallStatus.PENDING,\n   345→            created=datetime.now(),\n   346→            source=source,\n   347→            title=title,\n   348→            context=context,\n   349→            metadata=metadata or {},\n   350→        )\n   351→\n   352→        # Update tracking\n   353→        self._file_hashes[str(filepath)] = self._compute_file_hash(filepath)\n   354→        self._file_mtimes[str(filepath)] = filepath.stat().st_mtime\n   355→\n   356→        return call\n   357→\n   358→    def parse_call_file(self, filepath: Path) -> Optional[HumanCall]:\n   359→        \"\"\"Parse a human call file.\n   360→\n   361→        Args:\n   362→            filepath: Path to the call file\n   363→\n   364→        Returns:\n   365→            HumanCall object or None if parsing fails\n   366→        \"\"\"\n   367→        try:\n   368→            content = filepath.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n   369→            frontmatter, body = self._parse_frontmatter(content)\n   370→\n   371→            call_id = frontmatter.get(\"id\") or filepath.stem\n   372→\n   373→            # Determine status from file suffix or frontmatter\n   374→            status = CallStatus(frontmatter.get(\"status\", \"pending\"))\n   375→            if filepath.suffix == \".responded\" or filepath.name.endswith(\".responded.md\"):\n   376→                status = CallStatus.RESPONDED\n   377→            elif filepath.suffix == \".processing\" or filepath.name.endswith(\".processing.md\"):\n   378→                status = CallStatus.PROCESSING\n   379→\n   380→            # Extract response if present\n   381→            response = self._extract_section(body, self.RESPONSE_HEADERS)\n   382→            response_timestamp = None\n   383→\n   384→            # If we have a meaningful response, update status\n   385→            if self._has_meaningful_response(response):\n   386→                status = CallStatus.RESPONDED\n   387→                # Try to get response timestamp from file mtime\n   388→                stat = filepath.stat()\n   389→                response_timestamp = datetime.fromtimestamp(stat.st_mtime, tz=timezone.utc)\n   390→\n   391→            # Parse created timestamp\n   392→            created_str = frontmatter.get(\"created\", \"\")\n   393→            try:\n   394→                if created_str:\n   395→                    created = datetime.fromisoformat(created_str)\n   396→                    # Ensure timezone-aware (default to UTC if naive)\n   397→                    if created.tzinfo is None:\n   398→                        created = created.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n   399→                else:\n   400→                    created = datetime.fromtimestamp(filepath.stat().st_ctime, tz=timezone.utc)\n   401→            except ValueError:\n   402→                created = datetime.fromtimestamp(filepath.stat().st_ctime, tz=timezone.utc)\n   403→\n   404→            return HumanCall(\n   405→                id=call_id,\n   406→                file_path=filepath,\n   407→                call_type=CallType(frontmatter.get(\"type\", \"action\")),\n   408→                priority=CallPriority(frontmatter.get(\"priority\", \"medium\")),\n   409→                status=status,\n   410→                created=created,\n   411→                source=frontmatter.get(\"source\", \"unknown\"),\n   412→                title=self._extract_title(body) or filepath.stem,\n   413→                context=self._extract_section(body, self.CONTEXT_HEADERS),\n   414→                response=response,\n   415→                response_timestamp=response_timestamp,\n   416→                metadata={k: v for k, v in frontmatter.items() if k not in [\"id\", \"type\", \"priority\", \"status\", \"created\", \"source\", \"language\"]},\n   417→            )\n   418→        except (IOError, ValueError, KeyError) as e:\n   419→            return None\n   420→\n   421→    def _extract_title(self, body: str) -> str:\n   422→        \"\"\"Extract title from markdown body.\"\"\"\n   423→        match = re.search(r'^## Request:\\s*(.+)$', body, re.MULTILINE)\n   424→        if match:\n   425→            return match.group(1).strip()\n   426→        # Fallback: look for any level 2 heading\n   427→        match = re.search(r'^##\\s*(.+)$', body, re.MULTILINE)\n   428→        if match:\n   429→            return match.group(1).strip()\n   430→        return \"\"\n   431→\n   432→    def get_all_calls(self, include_completed: bool = False) -> List[HumanCall]:\n   433→        \"\"\"Get all human calls.\n   434→\n   435→        Args:\n   436→            include_completed: Whether to include completed calls\n   437→\n   438→        Returns:\n   439→            List of HumanCall objects\n   440→        \"\"\"\n   441→        calls = []\n   442→\n   443→        for filepath in self.calls_dir.glob(self.CALL_FILE_PATTERN):\n   444→            # Skip non-call files\n   445→            if not filepath.is_file():\n   446→                continue\n   447→\n   448→            call = self.parse_call_file(filepath)\n   449→            if call:\n   450→                if not include_completed and call.status in (CallStatus.COMPLETED, CallStatus.EXPIRED):\n   451→                    continue\n   452→                calls.append(call)\n   453→\n   454→        return sorted(calls, key=lambda c: c.created, reverse=True)\n   455→\n   456→    def get_pending_calls(self) -> List[HumanCall]:\n   457→        \"\"\"Get all pending calls (no response yet).\"\"\"\n   458→        return [c for c in self.get_all_calls() if c.status == CallStatus.PENDING]\n   459→\n   460→    def get_responded_calls(self) -> List[HumanCall]:\n   461→        \"\"\"Get all calls with responses waiting to be processed.\"\"\"\n   462→        return [c for c in self.get_all_calls() if c.status == CallStatus.RESPONDED]\n   463→\n   464→    def get_changed_calls(self, force_rescan: bool = False) -> List[HumanCall]:\n   465→        \"\"\"Get calls that have changed since last scan.\n   466→\n   467→        Optimized change detection using:\n   468→        - File system metadata (mtime) for fast checks\n   469→        - Caching parsed calls for repeated access\n   470→        - Batch processing for efficiency\n   471→\n   472→        Args:\n   473→            force_rescan: Force a full rescan even if no changes detected\n   474→\n   475→        Returns:\n   476→            List of changed HumanCall objects\n   477→        \"\"\"\n   478→        changed = []\n   479→        current_files = set()\n   480→\n   481→        for filepath in self.calls_dir.glob(self.CALL_FILE_PATTERN):\n   482→            if not filepath.is_file():\n   483→                continue\n   484→\n   485→            path_str = str(filepath)\n   486→            current_files.add(path_str)\n   487→            current_mtime = filepath.stat().st_mtime\n   488→\n   489→            # Check if file is new or changed\n   490→            is_new = path_str not in self._file_mtimes\n   491→            is_modified = (\n   492→                path_str in self._file_mtimes and\n   493→                self._file_mtimes[path_str] != current_mtime\n   494→            )\n   495→\n   496→            if is_new or is_modified or force_rescan:\n   497→                # Compute hash only if mtime changed (optimization)\n   498→                current_hash = self._compute_file_hash(filepath)\n   499→                content_changed = (\n   500→                    path_str in self._file_hashes and\n   501→                    self._file_hashes[path_str] != current_hash\n   502→                )\n   503→\n   504→                if is_new or content_changed or force_rescan:\n   505→                    call = self.parse_call_file(filepath)\n   506→                    if call:\n   507→                        changed.append(call)\n   508→                        self._call_cache[path_str] = call\n   509→                self._file_hashes[path_str] = current_hash\n   510→\n   511→            # Update tracking\n   512→            self._file_mtimes[path_str] = current_mtime\n   513→\n   514→        # Handle deleted files\n   515→        for path_str in list(self._file_mtimes.keys()):\n   516→            if path_str not in current_files:\n   517→                del self._file_mtimes[path_str]\n   518→                if path_str in self._file_hashes:\n   519→                    del self._file_hashes[path_str]\n   520→                if path_str in self._call_cache:\n   521→                    del self._call_cache[path_str]\n   522→\n   523→        self._last_scan_time = datetime.now()\n   524→        return changed\n   525→\n   526→    def get_cached_call(self, filepath: Path) -> Optional[HumanCall]:\n   527→        \"\"\"Get a call from cache or parse it if not cached.\n   528→\n   529→        Args:\n   530→            filepath: Path to the call file\n   531→\n   532→        Returns:\n   533→            Cached or parsed HumanCall object\n   534→        \"\"\"\n   535→        path_str = str(filepath)\n   536→        if path_str in self._call_cache:\n   537→            # Check if file has been modified since last cache\n   538→            current_mtime = filepath.stat().st_mtime\n   539→            if self._file_mtimes.get(path_str, 0) == current_mtime:\n   540→                return self._call_cache[path_str]\n   541→\n   542→        # Parse and cache\n   543→        call = self.parse_call_file(filepath)\n   544→        if call:\n   545→            self._call_cache[path_str] = call\n   546→            self._file_mtimes[path_str] = filepath.stat().st_mtime\n   547→            self._file_hashes[path_str] = self._compute_file_hash(filepath)\n   548→        return call\n   549→\n   550→    def mark_processing(self, call: HumanCall) -> None:\n   551→        \"\"\"Mark a call as being processed.\n   552→\n   553→        Args:\n   554→            call: The call to mark\n   555→        \"\"\"\n   556→        call.status = CallStatus.PROCESSING\n   557→        new_path = call.file_path.with_suffix(\".processing.md\")\n   558→\n   559→        # Rename file to indicate processing state\n   560→        if call.file_path.exists():\n   561→            call.file_path.rename(new_path)\n   562→            call.file_path = new_path\n   563→\n   564→        # Update tracking\n   565→        old_path_str = str(call.file_path.with_suffix(\".md\"))\n   566→        if old_path_str in self._file_hashes:\n   567→            del self._file_hashes[old_path_str]\n   568→        if old_path_str in self._file_mtimes:\n   569→            del self._file_mtimes[old_path_str]\n   570→        if old_path_str in self._call_cache:\n   571→            del self._call_cache[old_path_str]\n   572→\n   573→        self._file_hashes[str(new_path)] = self._compute_file_hash(new_path)\n   574→        self._file_mtimes[str(new_path)] = new_path.stat().st_mtime\n   575→        self._call_cache[str(new_path)] = call\n   576→\n   577→    def mark_completed(self, call: HumanCall) -> None:\n   578→        \"\"\"Mark a call as completed.\n   579→\n   580→        Args:\n   581→            call: The call to mark\n   582→        \"\"\"\n   583→        call.status = CallStatus.COMPLETED\n   584→        new_path = call.file_path.with_suffix(\".completed.md\")\n   585→\n   586→        # Rename file to indicate completed state\n   587→        if call.file_path.exists():\n   588→            call.file_path.rename(new_path)\n   589→            call.file_path = new_path\n   590→\n   591→        # Update tracking\n   592→        old_path_str = str(call.file_path.with_suffix(\".processing.md\"))\n   593→        if old_path_str in self._file_hashes:\n   594→            del self._file_hashes[old_path_str]\n   595→        if old_path_str in self._file_mtimes:\n   596→            del self._file_mtimes[old_path_str]\n   597→        if old_path_str in self._call_cache:\n   598→            del self._call_cache[old_path_str]\n   599→\n   600→        self._call_cache[str(new_path)] = call\n   601→\n   602→    def process_responded_calls(self, processor: Callable[[HumanCall], bool]) -> List[HumanCall]:\n   603→        \"\"\"Process all responded calls with a custom processor.\n   604→\n   605→        Args:\n   606→            processor: Function to process each call. Returns True if processing succeeded.\n   607→\n   608→        Returns:\n   609→            List of calls that were successfully processed\n   610→        \"\"\"\n   611→        processed = []\n   612→        responded_calls = self.get_responded_calls()\n   613→\n   614→        for call in responded_calls:\n   615→            self.mark_processing(call)\n   616→            try:\n   617→                success = processor(call)\n   618→                if success:\n   619→                    self.mark_completed(call)\n   620→                    processed.append(call)\n   621→                else:\n   622→                    # Revert to responded state if processing failed\n   623→                    self._revert_to_responded(call)\n   624→            except Exception as e:\n   625→                self._revert_to_responded(call)\n   626→                raise e\n   627→\n   628→        return processed\n   629→\n   630→    def _revert_to_responded(self, call: HumanCall) -> None:\n   631→        \"\"\"Revert a call from processing state to responded state.\n   632→\n   633→        Args:\n   634→            call: The call to revert\n   635→        \"\"\"\n   636→        call.status = CallStatus.RESPONDED\n   637→        new_path = call.file_path.with_suffix(\".md\")\n   638→\n   639→        if call.file_path.exists():\n   640→            call.file_path.rename(new_path)\n   641→            call.file_path = new_path\n   642→\n   643→        # Update tracking\n   644→        self._file_hashes[str(new_path)] = self._compute_file_hash(new_path)\n   645→        self._file_mtimes[str(new_path)] = new_path.stat().st_mtime\n   646→        self._call_cache[str(new_path)] = call\n   647→\n   648→    def batch_validate_responses(self, calls: List[HumanCall]) -> List[Tuple[HumanCall, bool, str]]:\n   649→        \"\"\"Validate multiple responses in batch.\n   650→\n   651→        Args:\n   652→            calls: List of calls to validate\n   653→\n   654→        Returns:\n   655→            List of (call, is_valid, reason) tuples\n   656→        \"\"\"\n   657→        results = []\n   658→        for call in calls:\n   659→            is_valid, reason = self.validate_response(call)\n   660→            results.append((call, is_valid, reason))\n   661→        return results\n   662→\n   663→    def validate_response(self, call: HumanCall) -> Tuple[bool, str]:\n   664→        \"\"\"Validate a human response for completeness and accuracy.\n   665→\n   666→        Comprehensive validation including:\n   667→        - Presence of response content\n   668→        - Absence of default prompt markers\n   669→        - Length checks (minimum and maximum)\n   670→        - Content quality checks\n   671→        - Structural validity\n   672→\n   673→        Args:\n   674→            call: The call to validate\n   675→\n   676→        Returns:\n   677→            Tuple of (is_valid, reason)\n   678→        \"\"\"\n   679→        if not call.response:\n   680→            return False, \"No response content\"\n   681→\n   682→        # Check for default prompt markers\n   683→        for marker in self.DEFAULT_PROMPT_MARKERS:\n   684→            if marker in call.response:\n   685→                return False, \"Response contains default prompt marker\"\n   686→\n   687→        # Clean response by removing comments\n   688→        cleaned = re.sub(r'<!--.*?-->', '', call.response, flags=re.DOTALL).strip()\n   689→\n   690→        # Check minimum length\n   691→        if len(cleaned) < self.MIN_RESPONSE_LENGTH:\n   692→            return False, f\"Response too short ({len(cleaned)} chars, minimum {self.MIN_RESPONSE_LENGTH})\"\n   693→\n   694→        # Check maximum length\n   695→        if len(cleaned) > self.MAX_RESPONSE_LENGTH:\n   696→            return False, f\"Response too long ({len(cleaned)} chars, maximum {self.MAX_RESPONSE_LENGTH})\"\n   697→\n   698→        # Check for meaningful content (not just whitespace or punctuation)\n   699→        meaningful_chars = re.sub(r'[\\s\\W]', '', cleaned)\n   700→        if len(meaningful_chars) < self.MIN_MEANINGFUL_CHARS:\n   701→            return False, \"Response lacks meaningful content\"\n   702→\n   703→        # Check for repetitive content\n   704→        if self._is_repetitive(cleaned):\n   705→            return False, \"Response contains repetitive or boilerplate content\"\n   706→\n   707→        # Check for valid response structure\n   708→        if not self._has_valid_structure(cleaned):\n   709→            return False, \"Response has invalid structure\"\n   710→\n   711→        return True, \"Response is valid\"\n   712→\n   713→    def _is_repetitive(self, content: str) -> bool:\n   714→        \"\"\"Check if content is repetitive or boilerplate.\n   715→\n   716→        Args:\n   717→            content: Response content to check\n   718→\n   719→        Returns:\n   720→            True if content is repetitive\n   721→        \"\"\"\n   722→        # Check for repeated patterns\n   723→        patterns = [\n   724→            r'(\\w+)(\\s+\\1){3,}',  # Same word repeated 4+ times\n   725→            r'(.{5,})(\\1){2,}',    # 5+ char sequence repeated 3+ times\n   726→        ]\n   727→\n   728→        for pattern in patterns:\n   729→            if re.search(pattern, content, re.IGNORECASE):\n   730→                return True\n   731→\n   732→        # Check for excessive punctuation\n   733→        punctuation_ratio = sum(1 for c in content if c in '.,!?;:') / len(content)\n   734→        if punctuation_ratio > 0.3:\n   735→            return True\n   736→\n   737→        return False\n   738→\n   739→    def _has_valid_structure(self, content: str) -> bool:\n   740→        \"\"\"Check if response has a valid structure.\n   741→\n   742→        Args:\n   743→            content: Response content to check\n   744→\n   745→        Returns:\n   746→            True if content has valid structure\n   747→        \"\"\"\n   748→        # At least one sentence with subject and verb structure\n   749→        # Simple check for common sentence patterns\n   750→        has_sentence = re.search(r'[A-Za-z]\\w*.*?[.!?]', content)\n   751→        if has_sentence:\n   752→            return True\n   753→\n   754→        # For non-English responses, check for basic structure\n   755→        if len(re.sub(r'[\\s\\W]', '', content)) >= 10:\n   756→            return True\n   757→\n   758→        return False\n   759→\n   760→    def get_stale_calls(self, timeout_days: int = 7) -> List[HumanCall]:\n   761→        \"\"\"Get calls that have been pending for too long.\n   762→\n   763→        Args:\n   764→            timeout_days: Days after which a call is considered stale\n   765→\n   766→        Returns:\n   767→            List of stale HumanCall objects\n   768→        \"\"\"\n   769→        cutoff = datetime.now(timezone.utc) - timedelta(days=timeout_days)\n   770→        return [\n   771→            c for c in self.get_all_calls()\n   772→            if c.status == CallStatus.PENDING and c.created < cutoff\n   773→        ]\n   774→\n   775→    def export_to_json(self, output_path: Path, include_completed: bool = False) -> None:\n   776→        \"\"\"Export all calls to JSON.\n   777→\n   778→        Args:\n   779→            output_path: Path to write JSON file\n   780→            include_completed: Whether to include completed calls\n   781→        \"\"\"\n   782→        calls = [c.to_dict() for c in self.get_all_calls(include_completed)]\n   783→        output_path.write_text(json.dumps(calls, indent=2, default=str), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n   784→\n   785→\n   786→# Backwards compatibility: maintain the old discover_human_calls function\n   787→def discover_human_calls(path: str = \"human-calls\") -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n   788→    \"\"\"Discover all human call files and their status.\n   789→\n   790→    Legacy compatibility function. Uses the new HumanCallStore internally.\n   791→\n   792→    Args:\n   793→        path: Path to human-calls directory\n   794→\n   795→    Returns:\n   796→        List of dicts with file info and parsed frontmatter\n   797→    \"\"\"\n   798→    store = HumanCallStore(Path(path))\n   799→    calls = store.get_all_calls(include_completed=True)\n   800→\n   801→    result = []\n   802→    for call in calls:\n   803→        result.append({\n   804→            'file': call.file_path.name,\n   805→            'path': str(call.file_path),\n   806→            'type': call.call_type.value,\n   807→            'priority': call.priority.value,\n   808→            'status': call.status.value,\n   809→            'created': call.created.strftime('%Y-%m-%d'),\n   810→            'title': call.title,\n   811→        })\n   812→\n   813→    return result\n   814→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fda141f5-a3a9-4f60-9302-36b25383cb2b","uuid":"cfa541ec-4d85-4dd6-82cc-2d71420ec27f","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/data/cre/workspace/se3.0/.worktrees/human-input-methods/tools/se3_tools/human_calls.py","content":"\"\"\"Human calls detection and processing module for SE 3.0.\n\nProvides optimized human call file handling with:\n- Structured storage format with frontmatter\n- Efficient change-based detection using file timestamps\n- Response integrity validation\n- Multi-language support\n\"\"\"\n\nimport re\nimport os\nimport json\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field, asdict\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\nfrom enum import Enum\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Optional, Any, Callable, Set, Tuple\nimport hashlib\n\n\nclass CallStatus(Enum):\n    \"\"\"Human call status states.\"\"\"\n    PENDING = \"pending\"\n    RESPONDED = \"responded\"\n    PROCESSING = \"processing\"\n    COMPLETED = \"completed\"\n    EXPIRED = \"expired\"\n\n\nclass CallType(Enum):\n    \"\"\"Human call types.\"\"\"\n    DECISION = \"decision\"\n    ACTION = \"action\"\n    INFORMATION = \"information\"\n    ESCALATION = \"escalation\"\n\n\nclass CallPriority(Enum):\n    \"\"\"Human call priority levels.\"\"\"\n    LOW = \"low\"\n    MEDIUM = \"medium\"\n    HIGH = \"high\"\n    CRITICAL = \"critical\"\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass HumanCall:\n    \"\"\"Represents a human call with metadata and content.\n\n    Attributes:\n        id: Unique identifier for the call\n        file_path: Path to the call file\n        call_type: Type of call (decision, action, information, escalation)\n        priority: Priority level\n        status: Current status\n        created: Creation timestamp\n        source: Source component (e.g., collab-orchestrator, worker)\n        title: Call title/subject\n        context: Call context/description\n        response: Human response content\n        response_timestamp: When response was received\n        metadata: Additional metadata\n    \"\"\"\n    id: str\n    file_path: Path\n    call_type: CallType = CallType.ACTION\n    priority: CallPriority = CallPriority.MEDIUM\n    status: CallStatus = CallStatus.PENDING\n    created: datetime = field(default_factory=datetime.now)\n    source: str = \"unknown\"\n    title: str = \"\"\n    context: str = \"\"\n    response: str = \"\"\n    response_timestamp: Optional[datetime] = None\n    metadata: Dict[str, Any] = field(default_factory=dict)\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        \"\"\"Convert to dictionary for serialization.\"\"\"\n        return {\n            \"id\": self.id,\n            \"file_path\": str(self.file_path),\n            \"type\": self.call_type.value,\n            \"priority\": self.priority.value,\n            \"status\": self.status.value,\n            \"created\": self.created.isoformat(),\n            \"source\": self.source,\n            \"title\": self.title,\n            \"context\": self.context,\n            \"response\": self.response,\n            \"response_timestamp\": self.response_timestamp.isoformat() if self.response_timestamp else None,\n            \"metadata\": self.metadata,\n        }\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_dict(cls, data: Dict[str, Any]) -> \"HumanCall\":\n        \"\"\"Create from dictionary.\"\"\"\n        return cls(\n            id=data[\"id\"],\n            file_path=Path(data[\"file_path\"]),\n            call_type=CallType(data.get(\"type\", \"action\")),\n            priority=CallPriority(data.get(\"priority\", \"medium\")),\n            status=CallStatus(data.get(\"status\", \"pending\")),\n            created=datetime.fromisoformat(data[\"created\"]) if \"created\" in data else datetime.now(),\n            source=data.get(\"source\", \"unknown\"),\n            title=data.get(\"title\", \"\"),\n            context=data.get(\"context\", \"\"),\n            response=data.get(\"response\", \"\"),\n            response_timestamp=datetime.fromisoformat(data[\"response_timestamp\"]) if data.get(\"response_timestamp\") else None,\n            metadata=data.get(\"metadata\", {}),\n        )\n\n\nclass HumanCallStore:\n    \"\"\"Manages human call files with optimized detection.\n\n    Features:\n    - Efficient change detection using file system events and caching\n    - Structured frontmatter format\n    - Comprehensive response integrity validation\n    - Multi-language support\n    - Batch processing capabilities\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # File patterns\n    CALL_FILE_PATTERN = \"*.md\"\n    RESPONDED_SUFFIX = \".responded\"\n    PROCESSING_SUFFIX = \".processing\"\n    COMPLETED_SUFFIX = \".completed\"\n\n    # Response section headers (multi-language)\n    RESPONSE_HEADERS = [\"### Response\", \"### 回复\", \"### Réponse\"]\n    CONTEXT_HEADERS = [\"### Context\", \"### 上下文\", \"### Contexte\"]\n\n    # Default prompt markers that indicate no response yet\n    DEFAULT_PROMPT_MARKERS = [\n        \"<!-- Human: write your response below -->\",\n        \"<!-- 人类：请在下方输入您的回复 -->\",\n        \"<!-- Humain: écrivez votre réponse ci-dessous -->\",\n    ]\n\n    # Minimum response requirements\n    MIN_RESPONSE_LENGTH = 10\n    MIN_MEANINGFUL_CHARS = 5\n    MAX_RESPONSE_LENGTH = 10000\n\n    def __init__(self, calls_dir: Path):\n        \"\"\"Initialize the store.\n\n        Args:\n            calls_dir: Directory containing human call files\n        \"\"\"\n        self.calls_dir = Path(calls_dir)\n        self.calls_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\n        # State tracking for efficient change detection\n        self._last_scan_time: Optional[datetime] = None\n        self._file_hashes: Dict[str, str] = {}\n        self._file_mtimes: Dict[str, float] = {}\n        self._call_cache: Dict[str, HumanCall] = {}\n\n        # Pre-scan to populate initial state\n        self._initialize_cache()\n\n    def _initialize_cache(self):\n        \"\"\"Initialize cache with existing call files.\"\"\"\n        for filepath in self.calls_dir.glob(self.CALL_FILE_PATTERN):\n            if filepath.is_file():\n                path_str = str(filepath)\n                self._file_mtimes[path_str] = filepath.stat().st_mtime\n                self._file_hashes[path_str] = self._compute_file_hash(filepath)\n                call = self.parse_call_file(filepath)\n                if call:\n                    self._call_cache[path_str] = call\n        self._last_scan_time = datetime.now()\n\n    def _compute_file_hash(self, filepath: Path) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Compute hash of file content for change detection.\n\n        Optimized to read only first 1KB for faster hash computation\n        \"\"\"\n        with open(filepath, 'rb') as f:\n            content = f.read(1024)  # Read first 1KB for faster hashing\n            return hashlib.sha256(content).hexdigest()[:16]\n\n    def _parse_frontmatter(self, content: str) -> Tuple[Dict[str, Any], str]:\n        \"\"\"Parse YAML-like frontmatter from markdown content.\n\n        Returns:\n            Tuple of (frontmatter dict, body content)\n        \"\"\"\n        frontmatter = {}\n        body = content\n\n        # Match frontmatter between --- markers\n        match = re.match(r'^---\\s*\\n(.*?)\\n---\\s*\\n(.*)', content, re.DOTALL)\n        if match:\n            fm_text = match.group(1)\n            body = match.group(2)\n\n            # Parse key: value pairs\n            for line in fm_text.strip().split('\\n'):\n                if ':' in line:\n                    key, value = line.split(':', 1)\n                    frontmatter[key.strip()] = value.strip()\n\n        return frontmatter, body\n\n    def _extract_section(self, content: str, headers: List[str]) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Extract content under a section header.\n\n        Args:\n            content: Full markdown content\n            headers: List of possible section headers to match\n\n        Returns:\n            Section content or empty string if not found\n        \"\"\"\n        lines = content.split('\\n')\n        in_section = False\n        section_lines = []\n\n        for line in lines:\n            # Check if this is the target section header\n            if any(line.strip().startswith(header) for header in headers):\n                in_section = True\n                continue\n\n            # Check if we've reached the next section\n            if in_section and line.strip().startswith('### '):\n                break\n\n            if in_section:\n                section_lines.append(line)\n\n        return '\\n'.join(section_lines).strip()\n\n    def _has_meaningful_response(self, content: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Check if content contains a meaningful human response.\n\n        Args:\n            content: Response section content\n\n        Returns:\n            True if response appears meaningful, False otherwise\n        \"\"\"\n        if not content:\n            return False\n\n        # Check for default prompt markers (indicates no real response)\n        for marker in self.DEFAULT_PROMPT_MARKERS:\n            if marker in content:\n                return False\n\n        # Check for HTML comments only (empty response)\n        cleaned = re.sub(r'<!--.*?-->', '', content, flags=re.DOTALL).strip()\n        if not cleaned:\n            return False\n\n        # Check minimum meaningful content length (at least 10 chars)\n        if len(cleaned) < 10:\n            return False\n\n        return True\n\n    def _generate_call_id(self, title: str, timestamp: Optional[datetime] = None) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Generate a unique call ID.\n\n        Format: {YYYYMMDD}-{HHmmss}-{short-description}\n        \"\"\"\n        ts = timestamp or datetime.now()\n        # Clean title for filename\n        clean_title = re.sub(r'[^\\w\\s-]', '', title.lower())\n        clean_title = re.sub(r'[-\\s]+', '-', clean_title).strip('-')[:30]\n        return f\"{ts.strftime('%Y%m%d-%H%M%S')}-{clean_title}\"\n\n    def create_call(\n        self,\n        title: str,\n        context: str,\n        call_type: CallType = CallType.ACTION,\n        priority: CallPriority = CallPriority.MEDIUM,\n        source: str = \"unknown\",\n        language: str = \"en\",\n        metadata: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None,\n    ) -> HumanCall:\n        \"\"\"Create a new human call file.\n\n        Args:\n            title: Call title\n            context: Call context/description\n            call_type: Type of call\n            priority: Priority level\n            source: Source component\n            language: Language code (en, zh, etc.)\n            metadata: Additional metadata\n\n        Returns:\n            Created HumanCall object\n        \"\"\"\n        call_id = self._generate_call_id(title)\n        filepath = self.calls_dir / f\"{call_id}.md\"\n\n        # Load language labels from config module\n        from .config import get_language_labels, is_chinese_language\n        t = get_language_labels(language)\n\n        # Add language guidance for context content\n        if is_chinese_language(language):\n            language_note = \"\\n\\n**注意**：请用中文回复。\"\n        else:\n            language_note = \"\"\n\n        # Build frontmatter and content\n        content = f\"\"\"---\nid: {call_id}\ntype: {call_type.value}\npriority: {priority.value}\nstatus: pending\ncreated: {datetime.now().isoformat()}\nsource: {source}\nlanguage: {language}\n---\n\n## Request: {title}\n\n**{t['type']}**: {call_type.value}\n**{t['urgency']}**: {priority.value}\n**{t['source']}**: {source}\n\n### {t['context']}\n{context}{language_note}\n\n### {t['response']}\n{t['prompt']}\n\"\"\"\n\n        filepath.write_text(content, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n        call = HumanCall(\n            id=call_id,\n            file_path=filepath,\n            call_type=call_type,\n            priority=priority,\n            status=CallStatus.PENDING,\n            created=datetime.now(),\n            source=source,\n            title=title,\n            context=context,\n            metadata=metadata or {},\n        )\n\n        # Update tracking\n        self._file_hashes[str(filepath)] = self._compute_file_hash(filepath)\n        self._file_mtimes[str(filepath)] = filepath.stat().st_mtime\n\n        return call\n\n    def parse_call_file(self, filepath: Path) -> Optional[HumanCall]:\n        \"\"\"Parse a human call file.\n\n        Args:\n            filepath: Path to the call file\n\n        Returns:\n            HumanCall object or None if parsing fails\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            content = filepath.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n            frontmatter, body = self._parse_frontmatter(content)\n\n            call_id = frontmatter.get(\"id\") or filepath.stem\n\n            # Determine status from file suffix or frontmatter\n            status = CallStatus(frontmatter.get(\"status\", \"pending\"))\n            if filepath.suffix == \".responded\" or filepath.name.endswith(\".responded.md\"):\n                status = CallStatus.RESPONDED\n            elif filepath.suffix == \".processing\" or filepath.name.endswith(\".processing.md\"):\n                status = CallStatus.PROCESSING\n\n            # Extract response if present\n            response = self._extract_section(body, self.RESPONSE_HEADERS)\n            response_timestamp = None\n\n            # If we have a meaningful response, update status\n            if self._has_meaningful_response(response):\n                status = CallStatus.RESPONDED\n                # Try to get response timestamp from file mtime\n                stat = filepath.stat()\n                response_timestamp = datetime.fromtimestamp(stat.st_mtime, tz=timezone.utc)\n\n            # Parse created timestamp\n            created_str = frontmatter.get(\"created\", \"\")\n            try:\n                if created_str:\n                    created = datetime.fromisoformat(created_str)\n                    # Ensure timezone-aware (default to UTC if naive)\n                    if created.tzinfo is None:\n                        created = created.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n                else:\n                    created = datetime.fromtimestamp(filepath.stat().st_ctime, tz=timezone.utc)\n            except ValueError:\n                created = datetime.fromtimestamp(filepath.stat().st_ctime, tz=timezone.utc)\n\n            return HumanCall(\n                id=call_id,\n                file_path=filepath,\n                call_type=CallType(frontmatter.get(\"type\", \"action\")),\n                priority=CallPriority(frontmatter.get(\"priority\", \"medium\")),\n                status=status,\n                created=created,\n                source=frontmatter.get(\"source\", \"unknown\"),\n                title=self._extract_title(body) or filepath.stem,\n                context=self._extract_section(body, self.CONTEXT_HEADERS),\n                response=response,\n                response_timestamp=response_timestamp,\n                metadata={k: v for k, v in frontmatter.items() if k not in [\"id\", \"type\", \"priority\", \"status\", \"created\", \"source\", \"language\"]},\n            )\n        except (IOError, ValueError, KeyError) as e:\n            return None\n\n    def _extract_title(self, body: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Extract title from markdown body.\"\"\"\n        match = re.search(r'^## Request:\\s*(.+)$', body, re.MULTILINE)\n        if match:\n            return match.group(1).strip()\n        # Fallback: look for any level 2 heading\n        match = re.search(r'^##\\s*(.+)$', body, re.MULTILINE)\n        if match:\n            return match.group(1).strip()\n        return \"\"\n\n    def get_all_calls(self, include_completed: bool = False) -> List[HumanCall]:\n        \"\"\"Get all human calls.\n\n        Args:\n            include_completed: Whether to include completed calls\n\n        Returns:\n            List of HumanCall objects\n        \"\"\"\n        calls = []\n\n        for filepath in self.calls_dir.glob(self.CALL_FILE_PATTERN):\n            # Skip non-call files\n            if not filepath.is_file():\n                continue\n\n            call = self.parse_call_file(filepath)\n            if call:\n                if not include_completed and call.status in (CallStatus.COMPLETED, CallStatus.EXPIRED):\n                    continue\n                calls.append(call)\n\n        return sorted(calls, key=lambda c: c.created, reverse=True)\n\n    def get_pending_calls(self) -> List[HumanCall]:\n        \"\"\"Get all pending calls (no response yet).\"\"\"\n        return [c for c in self.get_all_calls() if c.status == CallStatus.PENDING]\n\n    def get_responded_calls(self) -> List[HumanCall]:\n        \"\"\"Get all calls with responses waiting to be processed.\"\"\"\n        return [c for c in self.get_all_calls() if c.status == CallStatus.RESPONDED]\n\n    def get_changed_calls(self, force_rescan: bool = False) -> List[HumanCall]:\n        \"\"\"Get calls that have changed since last scan.\n\n        Optimized change detection using:\n        - File system metadata (mtime) for fast checks\n        - Caching parsed calls for repeated access\n        - Batch processing for efficiency\n\n        Args:\n            force_rescan: Force a full rescan even if no changes detected\n\n        Returns:\n            List of changed HumanCall objects\n        \"\"\"\n        changed = []\n        current_files = set()\n\n        for filepath in self.calls_dir.glob(self.CALL_FILE_PATTERN):\n            if not filepath.is_file():\n                continue\n\n            path_str = str(filepath)\n            current_files.add(path_str)\n            current_mtime = filepath.stat().st_mtime\n\n            # Check if file is new or changed\n            is_new = path_str not in self._file_mtimes\n            is_modified = (\n                path_str in self._file_mtimes and\n                self._file_mtimes[path_str] != current_mtime\n            )\n\n            if is_new or is_modified or force_rescan:\n                # Compute hash only if mtime changed (optimization)\n                current_hash = self._compute_file_hash(filepath)\n                content_changed = (\n                    path_str in self._file_hashes and\n                    self._file_hashes[path_str] != current_hash\n                )\n\n                if is_new or content_changed or force_rescan:\n                    call = self.parse_call_file(filepath)\n                    if call:\n                        changed.append(call)\n                        self._call_cache[path_str] = call\n                self._file_hashes[path_str] = current_hash\n\n            # Update tracking\n            self._file_mtimes[path_str] = current_mtime\n\n        # Handle deleted files\n        for path_str in list(self._file_mtimes.keys()):\n            if path_str not in current_files:\n                del self._file_mtimes[path_str]\n                if path_str in self._file_hashes:\n                    del self._file_hashes[path_str]\n                if path_str in self._call_cache:\n                    del self._call_cache[path_str]\n\n        self._last_scan_time = datetime.now()\n        return changed\n\n    def get_cached_call(self, filepath: Path) -> Optional[HumanCall]:\n        \"\"\"Get a call from cache or parse it if not cached.\n\n        Args:\n            filepath: Path to the call file\n\n        Returns:\n            Cached or parsed HumanCall object\n        \"\"\"\n        path_str = str(filepath)\n        if path_str in self._call_cache:\n            # Check if file has been modified since last cache\n            current_mtime = filepath.stat().st_mtime\n            if self._file_mtimes.get(path_str, 0) == current_mtime:\n                return self._call_cache[path_str]\n\n        # Parse and cache\n        call = self.parse_call_file(filepath)\n        if call:\n            self._call_cache[path_str] = call\n            self._file_mtimes[path_str] = filepath.stat().st_mtime\n            self._file_hashes[path_str] = self._compute_file_hash(filepath)\n        return call\n\n    def mark_processing(self, call: HumanCall) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Mark a call as being processed.\n\n        Args:\n            call: The call to mark\n        \"\"\"\n        call.status = CallStatus.PROCESSING\n        new_path = call.file_path.with_suffix(\".processing.md\")\n\n        # Rename file to indicate processing state\n        if call.file_path.exists():\n            call.file_path.rename(new_path)\n            call.file_path = new_path\n\n        # Update tracking\n        old_path_str = str(call.file_path.with_suffix(\".md\"))\n        if old_path_str in self._file_hashes:\n            del self._file_hashes[old_path_str]\n        if old_path_str in self._file_mtimes:\n            del self._file_mtimes[old_path_str]\n        if old_path_str in self._call_cache:\n            del self._call_cache[old_path_str]\n\n        self._file_hashes[str(new_path)] = self._compute_file_hash(new_path)\n        self._file_mtimes[str(new_path)] = new_path.stat().st_mtime\n        self._call_cache[str(new_path)] = call\n\n    def mark_completed(self, call: HumanCall) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Mark a call as completed.\n\n        Args:\n            call: The call to mark\n        \"\"\"\n        call.status = CallStatus.COMPLETED\n        new_path = call.file_path.with_suffix(\".completed.md\")\n\n        # Rename file to indicate completed state\n        if call.file_path.exists():\n            call.file_path.rename(new_path)\n            call.file_path = new_path\n\n        # Update tracking\n        old_path_str = str(call.file_path.with_suffix(\".processing.md\"))\n        if old_path_str in self._file_hashes:\n            del self._file_hashes[old_path_str]\n        if old_path_str in self._file_mtimes:\n            del self._file_mtimes[old_path_str]\n        if old_path_str in self._call_cache:\n            del self._call_cache[old_path_str]\n\n        self._call_cache[str(new_path)] = call\n\n    def process_responded_calls(self, processor: Callable[[HumanCall], bool]) -> List[HumanCall]:\n        \"\"\"Process all responded calls with a custom processor.\n\n        Args:\n            processor: Function to process each call. Returns True if processing succeeded.\n\n        Returns:\n            List of calls that were successfully processed\n        \"\"\"\n        processed = []\n        responded_calls = self.get_responded_calls()\n\n        for call in responded_calls:\n            self.mark_processing(call)\n            try:\n                success = processor(call)\n                if success:\n                    self.mark_completed(call)\n                    processed.append(call)\n                else:\n                    # Revert to responded state if processing failed\n                    self._revert_to_responded(call)\n            except Exception as e:\n                self._revert_to_responded(call)\n                raise e\n\n        return processed\n\n    def _revert_to_responded(self, call: HumanCall) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Revert a call from processing state to responded state.\n\n        Args:\n            call: The call to revert\n        \"\"\"\n        call.status = CallStatus.RESPONDED\n        new_path = call.file_path.with_suffix(\".md\")\n\n        if call.file_path.exists():\n            call.file_path.rename(new_path)\n            call.file_path = new_path\n\n        # Update tracking\n        self._file_hashes[str(new_path)] = self._compute_file_hash(new_path)\n        self._file_mtimes[str(new_path)] = new_path.stat().st_mtime\n        self._call_cache[str(new_path)] = call\n\n    def batch_validate_responses(self, calls: List[HumanCall]) -> List[Tuple[HumanCall, bool, str]]:\n        \"\"\"Validate multiple responses in batch.\n\n        Args:\n            calls: List of calls to validate\n\n        Returns:\n            List of (call, is_valid, reason) tuples\n        \"\"\"\n        results = []\n        for call in calls:\n            is_valid, reason = self.validate_response(call)\n            results.append((call, is_valid, reason))\n        return results\n\n    def validate_response(self, call: HumanCall) -> Tuple[bool, str]:\n        \"\"\"Validate a human response for completeness and accuracy.\n\n        Comprehensive validation including:\n        - Presence of response content\n        - Absence of default prompt markers\n        - Length checks (minimum and maximum)\n        - Content quality checks\n        - Structural validity\n\n        Args:\n            call: The call to validate\n\n        Returns:\n            Tuple of (is_valid, reason)\n        \"\"\"\n        if not call.response:\n            return False, \"No response content\"\n\n        # Check for default prompt markers\n        for marker in self.DEFAULT_PROMPT_MARKERS:\n            if marker in call.response:\n                return False, \"Response contains default prompt marker\"\n\n        # Clean response by removing comments\n        cleaned = re.sub(r'<!--.*?-->', '', call.response, flags=re.DOTALL).strip()\n\n        # Check minimum length\n        if len(cleaned) < self.MIN_RESPONSE_LENGTH:\n            return False, f\"Response too short ({len(cleaned)} chars, minimum {self.MIN_RESPONSE_LENGTH})\"\n\n        # Check maximum length\n        if len(cleaned) > self.MAX_RESPONSE_LENGTH:\n            return False, f\"Response too long ({len(cleaned)} chars, maximum {self.MAX_RESPONSE_LENGTH})\"\n\n        # Check for meaningful content (not just whitespace or punctuation)\n        meaningful_chars = re.sub(r'[\\s\\W]', '', cleaned)\n        if len(meaningful_chars) < self.MIN_MEANINGFUL_CHARS:\n            return False, \"Response lacks meaningful content\"\n\n        # Check for repetitive content\n        if self._is_repetitive(cleaned):\n            return False, \"Response contains repetitive or boilerplate content\"\n\n        # Check for valid response structure\n        if not self._has_valid_structure(cleaned):\n            return False, \"Response has invalid structure\"\n\n        return True, \"Response is valid\"\n\n    def _is_repetitive(self, content: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Check if content is repetitive or boilerplate.\n\n        Args:\n            content: Response content to check\n\n        Returns:\n            True if content is repetitive\n        \"\"\"\n        # Check for repeated patterns\n        patterns = [\n            r'(\\w+)(\\s+\\1){3,}',  # Same word repeated 4+ times\n            r'(.{5,})(\\1){2,}',    # 5+ char sequence repeated 3+ times\n        ]\n\n        for pattern in patterns:\n            if re.search(pattern, content, re.IGNORECASE):\n                return True\n\n        # Check for excessive punctuation\n        punctuation_ratio = sum(1 for c in content if c in '.,!?;:') / len(content)\n        if punctuation_ratio > 0.3:\n            return True\n\n        return False\n\n    def _has_valid_structure(self, content: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Check if response has a valid structure.\n\n        Args:\n            content: Response content to check\n\n        Returns:\n            True if content has valid structure\n        \"\"\"\n        # At least one sentence with subject and verb structure\n        # Simple check for common sentence patterns\n        has_sentence = re.search(r'[A-Za-z]\\w*.*?[.!?]', content)\n        if has_sentence:\n            return True\n\n        # For non-English responses, check for basic structure\n        if len(re.sub(r'[\\s\\W]', '', content)) >= 10:\n            return True\n\n        return False\n\n    def get_stale_calls(self, timeout_days: int = 7) -> List[HumanCall]:\n        \"\"\"Get calls that have been pending for too long.\n\n        Args:\n            timeout_days: Days after which a call is considered stale\n\n        Returns:\n            List of stale HumanCall objects\n        \"\"\"\n        cutoff = datetime.now(timezone.utc) - timedelta(days=timeout_days)\n        return [\n            c for c in self.get_all_calls()\n            if c.status == CallStatus.PENDING and c.created < cutoff\n        ]\n\n    def export_to_json(self, output_path: Path, include_completed: bool = False) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Export all calls to JSON.\n\n        Args:\n            output_path: Path to write JSON file\n            include_completed: Whether to include completed calls\n        \"\"\"\n        calls = [c.to_dict() for c in self.get_all_calls(include_completed)]\n        output_path.write_text(json.dumps(calls, indent=2, default=str), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n\n# Backwards compatibility: maintain the old discover_human_calls function\ndef discover_human_calls(path: str = \"human-calls\") -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Discover all human call files and their status.\n\n    Legacy compatibility function. Uses the new HumanCallStore internally.\n\n    Args:\n        path: Path to human-calls directory\n\n    Returns:\n        List of dicts with file info and parsed frontmatter\n    \"\"\"\n    store = HumanCallStore(Path(path))\n    calls = store.get_all_calls(include_completed=True)\n\n    result = []\n    for call in calls:\n        result.append({\n            'file': call.file_path.name,\n            'path': str(call.file_path),\n            'type': call.call_type.value,\n            'priority': call.priority.value,\n            'status': call.status.value,\n            'created': call.created.strftime('%Y-%m-%d'),\n            'title': call.title,\n        })\n\n    return result\n","numLines":814,"startLine":1,"totalLines":814}}}
